; Get the dictionary word for an id
;
; Reads the word offset for id A (bit 7 ignored) from the table #R$A20E (words,
; index from 1): 1-10 are the directions north .. down, 11 and up the object
; state words (unlocked, empty, off, closed, dead, locked, full, broken, on,
; open, alive). $A0BD does the same for another table in HL (the state word
; tables #R$A224 and #R$A234).
;
; A Id (bit 7 ignored)
; HL Table of words ($A0BD only; $A0BA uses #R$A20E)
; O:DE Word offset in the dictionary (print with #R$74C1); 0 for an id with no word
@label=GetIdWord
c$A0BA LD HL,$A20E
@label=GetTableWord
*$A0BD LD E,A
 $A0BE RES 7,E
 $A0C0 LD D,$00
 $A0C2 ADD HL,DE
 $A0C3 ADD HL,DE
 $A0C4 LD E,(HL)
 $A0C5 INC HL
 $A0C6 LD D,(HL)
 $A0C7 RET
